  "query": "A boat is at the current point. Write down the bearing that the boat should travel on to return to the starting point.",
  "answer": "N 34° W",
  "answer_type": "text",
  "subject": "PlaneGeometry",
  "level": "high_school",
  "provenance": {
    "source_key": "s2134",
    "source_answer": "N 34° W",
    "previous_model_response": "Take east as \\(x\\) and north as \\(y\\). The boat’s displacement from the start to the current is\n\n\\[\nx=12\\sin14^\\circ+16\\sin49^\\circ\\approx14.98\\text{ km},\n\\]\n\n\\[\ny=-(12\\cos14^\\circ+16\\cos49^\\circ)\\approx-22.14\\text{ km}.\n\\]\n\nTo return, the boat must travel \\(14.98\\) km west and \\(22.14\\) km north. The angle west of north is\n\n\\[\n\\theta=\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{14.98}{22.14}\\right)\\approx34.1^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nThus the bearing is \\(N34.1^\\circ W\\), or in three-figure form:\n\n\\[\n360^\\circ-34.1^\\circ=325.9^\\circ\\approx\\boxed{326^\\circ}.\n\\]\n\n326°"
  },
  "answer_verification": {
    "status": "verified",
    "verified_answer": "N 34 degrees W",
    "reasoning": "The two legs have east components 12 sin14? and 16 sin49?, and south components 12 cos14? and 16 cos49?. From the current point back to Start, the displacement is 22.1405 km north and 14.9784 km west, giving bearing N arctan(14.9784/22.1405) W = N34.1?W, matching the source answer rounded to a whole degree."
